.TH SDL_GetGamepadStringForButton 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetGamepadStringForButton \- Convert from an
.BR SDL_GamepadButton
enum to a string.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gamepad.h>
.PP
.BI "const char * SDL_GetGamepadStringForButton(SDL_GamepadButton button);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I button
an enum value for a given
.BR SDL_GamepadButton \[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a string for the given button, or NULL if an invalid button is specified\[char46] The string returned is of the format used by
.BR SDL_Gamepad
mapping strings\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

